CORE
s_until2.sv
--bound 3
^\[main\.p0\] always \(main\.s == 1 \|-> \(main\.s == 1 s_until main\.s == 2\)\): PROVED up to bound 3$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
When encoding until/R for lasso-shaped counterexamples,
property_obligations_rec (src/trans-word-level/property.cpp) previously
iterated over the time frames from min(current, lasso.start), i.e., it
included time frames before the current time frame when the loop started
earlier. The operands were hence evaluated in time frames that precede
the start of the evaluation attempt. With bound 3, the lasso from t=3
back to t=0 caused the attempt starting at t=1 to check the operands at
t=0, and EBMC reported REFUTED. Fixed by iterating the time frames in
path order starting at 'current' (current..end-1, then start..current-1),
which never visits a state preceding the start of the attempt.
